# Git and Commit Rules

## 🚫 AI Git Blacklist (CRITICAL)
- ❌ **NEVER RUN**: `git add`, `git commit`, `git push`, `git merge`, `git pull`
- ❌ **FORBIDDEN**: Any git command execution whatsoever
- ❌ **NO AUTOMATION**: Zero git interaction from AI
- ✅ **ONLY ALLOWED**: File modifications and code changes
- 👤 **USER CONTROL**: Human handles ALL git operations manually

## 📋 Commit Guidelines (For User)
- Make simple commits of no more than 10 words
- Use present tense (e.g. "Add contact validation", "Fix email provider")
- Be descriptive but concise
- One logical change per commit

## 🎯 AI Responsibilities
- ✅ Modify files as requested
- ✅ Suggest commit messages (but not execute)
- ✅ Prepare code for user to commit
- ❌ Never touch git commands
- 📢 Say "Ready for you to commit" when changes are done

## Examples
**Good commit messages:**
- "Add Mailgun webhook tracking"
- "Fix email provider priority"
- "Update user seeder"

**AI should say:**
- "File modified, ready for you to commit"
- "Changes complete, you can now commit"
- NOT: "Let me commit this for you"
